hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"110","Yuqra'u ((Alif Lam Mim Tanzil)) al-Sajdah, wa ((Tabaraka alladhi bi-yadihi al-mulk)).. Recite ((Alif Lam Mim Tanzil)) — Surah As-Sajdah, and ((Blessed is He in Whose Hand is the dominion)) — Surah Al-Mulk."
"111","Allahumma aslamtu nafsi ilayka, wa fawwadtu amri ilayka, wa wajjahtu wajhi ilayka, wa alja'tu dhahri ilayka, raghbatan wa rahbatan ilayka, la malja'a wa la manjaa minka illa ilayka, amantu bikitabika alladhi anzalta wa bi-nabiyyika alladhi arsalta.. O Allah, I have submitted my soul to You, entrusted my affairs to You, turned my face toward You, and placed my reliance upon You, out of hope in You and fear of You. There is no refuge and no escape from You except to You. I believe in Your Book which You have revealed and in Your Prophet whom You have sent."
